# Usage-metrics shards — git attribute rules.
#
# -diff: git renders a binary-file notice instead of shard content in every
# diff. This is the anti-Goodhart guard for the one channel a prompt-scanning
# grep cannot see. Three commands read working-tree diffs with an LLM in the
# loop, and without this rule a phase that touches these files would feed
# metric values straight into a reviewer's context:
#   - /relay-implement writes `git diff <base_commit>` into
#     PRPs/reports/<feature>/phase-<N>/attempts/<i>/diff.patch, then hands it to
#     the code-reviewer, the test-runner and the visual-verifier
#   - /relay-commit current-branch mode reviews `git diff` and `git diff --staged`
#   - /relay-qa-report diff mode derives cases from `git status --porcelain` + `git diff`
# Removing this line silently reopens all three.
#
# text eol=lf: the checkout-layer complement to the materializer's own literal
# '\n' line endings. Without it a Windows checkout reintroduces CRLF (git warns
# "LF will be replaced by CRLF the next time Git touches it"), which breaks the
# byte-identical-regeneration guarantee at a layer the script cannot control.

*.tsv -diff
*.tsv text eol=lf
